<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended marginally higher on Thursday after a quiet session but dealers said they believed bonos were still well supported.</p>
<p>&quot;The session was very quiet with U.S. markets closed but strength in bunds and the dollar against the mark kept a positive tone in the market,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>By the close the spread over German bunds was trading at 136 basis points versus 132 bps in early trade.</p>
</text>
